{{Skl|Farming}} is one of the [[Skills]] available for players to level up as they perform certain actions that give them '''Farming''' XP.

[[Roman Numerals]] are used to express its levels in-game.

Although Farming goes from levels {{Green|1–50}} (I – L) by default, there is {{Skill XP|+50 [[Farming]]}} required to reach the first level, meaning there is a "level 0", just like all other [[Skills]]. 

The [[Farming Level Cap]] can be increased through [[Jacob's Farming Contests]], to a maximum of Level 60 (LX). In order to reach this cap, players must place in the '''{{Gold|GOLD}}''' bracket of a unique crop type, then purchase the upgrade from {{NPCSprite|Anita}} in the {{Zone|Farmhouse}}. This can be done 10 times, increasing the cap one level for each unique crop type mastered.

== Mechanics ==
=== Public Islands ===
Farming on Public Islands serves mostly as an introduction to the skill and the means to unlock various collections. It ranges from the [[Hub Island]] (in the {{Zone|Village}}, {{zone|Mountain}} and {{zone|Farm}} areas), the [[Farming Islands]] (in {{Zone|The Barn}} and {{zone|Mushroom Desert}}, on the later of which are {{ID|Glowing Mushroom}}s) to the [[Crimson Isle]] (featuring {{ID|Nether Wart}} as well as the unique crops of {{ID|Mushroom Spore}}s and {{ID|Red Thornleaf}} which require {{ID|Spore Harvester}} and {{ID|Thornleaf Scythe}} respectively to be collected). More focused or thorough Farming is done better on the [[Garden]], if the crops allow it.

Inside the [[Rift Dimension]] players can also find the unique crops of {{ID|Riftwart Roots}}, {{ID|Agaricus Cap}}, {{ID|Caducous Stem}}, {{ID|Half-Eaten Carrot}} and {{ID|Wilted Berberis}}, which can only be harvested using the {{ID|Wand of Farming}}. Those crops cannot be planted on the Garden, but fortunately, comparatively fewer are required.

The [[Farming Islands]] also feature Animals, which grant '''Farming''' XP when slain, and have their own farming collections. Those cannot be grinded efficiently, and as such [[Minions]] are recommended. Although [[Animal Axes]] do exist, for those who wish to finish their collections manually.

=== Private Islands ===
{{Main|Garden}}
Before the release of [[Garden]], players would build Farms on their own islands, as it was significantly more efficient than Farming on public islands, whether it was for [[Collection]], Farming XP or {{c}}. The addition of Garden made the creation of Farms much easier and farming itself much more efficient.

Once it has been unlocked — which requires {{SkyBlock Level|5}} and is then accessed via {{NPCSprite|Sam}} who appears on player's [[Private Island]] — Farming on [[The Garden]] is the only viable way to Farm, as Public islands frequently have multiple people and don't allow for custom farms; and on [[Private Island]], player's {{stat|FmF}} is disabled. Unlocking plots on Garden requires {{ID|Compost}}, obtained from [[Composter]] and before being able to use unlocked plots, players first need to clean them. This can be done with vanilla tools or via {{ID|Sam's Scythe}}, {{ID|Garden Scythe}} or {{ID|Plot Eraser}}.

While Garden has presets for each of the crops, there are farms that can be built manually that are more efficient, whether it's because of their use of the space or by allowing the max number of Crops broken per second. Players can build Farms using tools such as {{ID|Builder's Wand}}, {{ID|Builder's Ruler}}, {{ID|InfiniDirt™ Wand}}, {{ID|Magical Water Bucket}} and {{ID|Block Zapper}}, as well as vanilla tools enchanted with {{Ench|Efficiency}}. 

Crops, similarly to vanilla Minecraft, require {{ID|Water}} to grow, they however don't require a light source. Crops each require a different [[w: Substrate (biology)|Substrate]], such as Tilted Dirt for {{ID|Wheat}} or {{ID|Carrot}}s, or {{ID|Soul Sand}} for {{ID|Nether Wart}}. Dirt can be tilted en masse via {{ID|Hoe of Great Tilling}}, {{ID|Hoe of Greater Tilling}} and {{ID|Hoe of Greatest Tilling}}. Crops can be planted manually or using {{ID|Basket of Seeds}} and {{ID|Nether Wart Pouch}}. {{ID|Red Mushroom!Red}} and {{ID|Brown Mushroom}}s however cannot be planted using these items and can only be done manually.

To prevent having to replant crops upon every harvest, players can use the {{Ench|Replenish}} enchantment, obtained from {{Coll|Cocoa Beans 8}}. Players can also use {{Ench|Delicate}}, obtained from {{NPCSprite|Anita}}, which prevents the breaking of Pumpkin and Melon stems, as well as crops that are not fully grown.
==== Farming Tools ====
{{Main|Farming Tools}}
There are {{Green|12}} unique Farming Tools. They can stored in the [[Farming Toolkit]], which is a Consumable purchased from [[SkyMart]] for {{Copper|500}}. Once consumed it can be accessed with {{code|/FarmingToolkit}}, by shift + right-clicking a tool that has been donated to the Toolkit, or through the storage menu.

Farming Tools are crop specific and grant extra {{stat|Crop Fortune}} to their specialised [[Crop]]. Farming Tools are leveled by gaining {{Skill|Farming|XP}} while farming using the Tool or by applying {{ID|Tool Exp Capsule}}s, these level the tool up to level {{Green|40}} by default. This limit can be increased to {{Green|50}} using a total of {{RD|10 Overclocker 3000}}s. Each Tool level increases its stats, and eventually also the amount of [[Gemstone Slots]] and rarity.

==== Pests ====
{{Main|Pests}}
By reaching {{Garden|5}}, players unlock a new unique mechanic — Pests. When farming on {{zone|Garden}}, one of 13 (one for every crop) pests may spawn. The same happens once for every hour of the Garden being unloaded. Up to {{Green|8}} can be spawned at the same time, and the more of them there are, the more is player's {{stat|FmF}} reduced. Players can use {{ID|Pest Repellent}} or {{ID|Pest Repellent MAX}} to slow their spawning, but it is recommended to instead kill them using [[Vacuums]], as each pest drops Crops as well as unique items which can help players farm. Additionally, by slaying Pests players obtain a special currency — {{Pests}} — which can be traded with {{NPCSprite|Phillip}} for Pest-related items.

==== Greenhouse ====
{{Main|Greenhouse}}
The [[Greenhouse]] is plot in [[The Garden]]. It can be accessed at {{Garden|7}} (VII) after accepting the {{NPCSprite|Carpenter}} as a [[The Garden#Visitor|Visitor]] in the Garden and obtaining the {{ID|Greenhouse Blueprint}}. 

The size of useable {{ID|Farmland}} inside the [[Greenhouse]] can be increased by using {{ID|Ethereal Vine}}s, which can be obtained when harvesting [[Mutations]] and [[Crops]] inside the [[Greenhouse]]. Up to {{Green|3}} [[Greenhouse]] plots can be placed at once.

Some [[Crops]] and [[Mutations]] require water while growing in the [[Greenhouse]]. They can be watered with the use of a {{ID|HydroCan™ 1000}} or its upgrades. If not watered, the plant has a chance to not grow, and if it reaches {{Green|0}}, die.

The status of plants within the [[Greenhouse]] can be viewed with a {{ID|Plant Diagnostics Tool}}.

====== Mutations ======
{{Main|Mutations}}
[[Mutations]] can be grown in the [[Greenhouse]] when [[Crops]] and other [[Mutations]] meet specific requirements within the [[Greenhouse]].

